// Copy to Config/Secrets.xcconfig (git-ignored) and fill in what you need; scripts/generate.sh
// does the copy on first run. Anything left out keeps its default from Config/Base.xcconfig.
// Every key here can instead be entered in the app (Settings), which keeps it in the Keychain
// and takes precedence over these. In-app entry is the safer choice: values set here are
// compiled into the app, where anyone holding the .ipa can read them.
// In an xcconfig "//" starts a comment, so write URLs as https:/$()/host.

// --- Your build ---
// For a device build, set your team. Change the bundle ID if you are signing your own fork.
// POLARIS_BUNDLE_ID = com.yourname.beeline
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
// POLARIS_CONTACT = https:/$()/github.com/yourname/beeline

// --- Keys (all optional) ---
// Google Routes API: console.cloud.google.com → enable "Routes API" → create an API key
// restricted to iOS apps with your POLARIS_BUNDLE_ID AND to the Routes API only. The
// bundle-ID check is just a header anyone can copy, so also cap its daily quota (Routes API
// → Quotas) and set a budget alert. That bounds the cost if the key ever leaks.
GOOGLE_ROUTES_API_KEY =
// TfL Unified API: api-portal.tfl.gov.uk → subscribe → primary key. Optional: TfL works
// without a key at a lower rate limit (50 requests a minute).
TFL_APP_KEY =

// --- Alerts for your lines (optional): your own server, see README "Run your own alerts server" ---
// POLARIS_ALERTS_URL = https:/$()/beeline-alerts.yourname.workers.dev
// A single phone's invitation. For distributed builds, enter it on the phone in Settings.
POLARIS_ALERTS_TOKEN =
